nputs is computationally universal in that copies of the gate can be “wired together” to effect any desired logic circuit, and to perform any desired unitary transformation on a set of quantum variables.", "abstract_source_suggest": {"input": "APS"}}], "refereed": true, "titles": [{"title": "Almost Any Quantum Logic Gate is Universal"}], "external_system_identifiers": [{"schema": "SPIRES", "value": "SPIRES-7995598"}], "facet_author_name": ["1024175_Seth Lloyd"], "_oai": {"sets": ["Literature"], "id": "oai:inspirehep.net:414874", "updated": "2025-06-06T17:30:59.838647"}, "curated": true, "journal_title_variants": ["Phys. Rev. Lett.", "Phys.Rev.Lett."]}}], "total": 1}, "links": {"self": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=doi%3A10.1103%2Fphysrevlett.75.346&size=5&page=1", "bibtex": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=doi%3A10.1103%2Fphysrevlett.75.346&size=5&page=1&format=bibtex", "latex-eu": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=doi%3A10.1103%2Fphysrevlett.75.346&size=5&page=1&format=latex-eu", "latex-us": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=doi%3A10.1103%2Fphysrevlett.75.346&size=5&page=1&format=latex-us", "json": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=doi%3A10.1103%2Fphysrevlett.75.346&size=5&page=1&format=json", "json-expanded": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=doi%3A10.1103%2Fphysrevlett.75.346&size=5&page=1&format=json-expanded", "cv": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=doi%3A10.1103%2Fphysrevlett.75.346&size=5&page=1&format=cv"}}